      "designer": "Anders Wikström",
      "description": "Loopy captures a kind of bubbly lettershapes that are familiar from comics, stickers and street art, but rarely seen in serious typography, and thus rarely given the attention to detail that they deserve. Systematically irregular, with sometimes looping outlines, Loopy is happily ignorant about logic or typographic etiquette.\n\nIt's a layered color typeface. You can combine styles with outline, highlight, shadow and fill, and set them in any colors you like.\n\nYou can do whatever. Do an invitation card, typeset a bible.\n\nLoopy is free software and open source.",
